What changed this round (landed)
- Landed code changes in:
  - `clang/aot/_.c`
  - `clang/aot/emit.c`
- Added expression-mode OP2 coverage (head=0 emitter path).
  - New `case OP2` in expression emission builds `term_new_op2(opr, lhs, rhs)`.
  - Both operands are captured lazily as ALO terms (no strict eval in expression mode).
  - Added residual reason `AOT_DEOPT_EXPR_OP2_LHS_CAPTURE` and kept `..._RHS_CAPTURE`.
  - This converts prior hard `EXPR_UNSUPPORTED_TAG` deopts at OP2 expression sites into `AOT_RESID` captures.
- Strengthened strict forcing used by compiled SWI/MAT scrutinees.
  - New limit: `AOT_FORCE_STRICT_FUEL=64`.
  - `aot_can_force_strict_tag` now includes `OP2` and `USE` (in addition to `APP/ALO/REF`).
  - `aot_force_strict` is now iterative:
    - repeatedly handles DP via `aot_force_dup`,
    - repeatedly WHNF-forces forceable tags via `aot_force_whnf_local`,
    - exits on no-progress or non-forceable tag.
  - Head-mode SWI/MAT emission now always calls `aot_force_strict(arg, *s_pos)` and writes back to the APP arg slot; it no longer gates forcing behind a fixed tag pre-check.

